From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: SetThreadIdealProcessor accepts up to MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS

SetThreadIdealProcessor refused 33 for a 32-bit program under wow64 (the
test of Windows' behaviour asks for a 32-bit MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS + 1 and
expects success); it only knew 32 and 64 as "no preference". Numbers up
to MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS are accepted now, those the machine has no processor
for only ask for the previous ideal processor, 65 and above are
STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER.

---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -2772,9 +2772,16 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetInformationThread( HANDLE handle, THREADINFOCLASS class,
         BOOL query;
 
         if (length != sizeof(*number)) return STATUS_INFO_LENGTH_MISMATCH;
-        /* a 32-bit program's MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS is 32 */
+        /* up to MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS is accepted (Windows' own wow64 test asks for
+         * 33, a 32-bit program's MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS + 1); a number the machine
+         * has no processor for, or MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS itself, only asks */
+        if (*number > MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS) return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_IDEAL_STRICT
         query = *number == MAXIMUM_PROCESSORS || (is_wow64() && *number == 32);
         if (!query && *number >= peb->NumberOfProcessors) return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+#else
+        query = *number >= peb->NumberOfProcessors;
+#endif
         if ((status = get_thread_settings( handle, TRUE, &thread_data ))) return status;
         previous = thread_data && thread_data->ideal_processor ? thread_data->ideal_processor - 1 : 0;
         if (thread_data && !query) thread_data->ideal_processor = *number + 1;
